You're correct, and I overstated the TTY thing. Let me correct it cleanly.

Session tracking has no TTY gate. It's driven entirely by hooks, all of which are now installed in .claude/settings.json and run non-interactively via sh -c:

SessionStart, SessionEnd, Stop → session lifecycle capture
UserPromptSubmit → captures each prompt
